# 2026-10-10 build-integration.sh clean smoke

## Failed attempt 1: two script instances

A second integration script was started while the first clean build still held
the Android build graph. The second instance deleted target output after its
Android lock probe timed out and caused the first build to race:

```text
Tried to lock out/.lock, but timed out polling every 1s until 10s
cp: bad 'out/target/product/OP64D3L1/system/etc/task_profiles.json': No such file or directory
```

The script now takes a separate exclusive
`out/.op64d3l1-build-integration.lock` before deleting any target output.

Lock regression test while a build was active:

```text
RC=2
ERROR: another OP64D3L1 integration build is using this source tree
```

## Failed attempt 2: gate scanned historical documentation

A recursive v17 interface grep matched this research archive after the image
build had completed. The gate now checks the staged target output and requires
the file to exist.

